  - target: term/dla-component-distinction
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The CA definition specifically identifies the highest or middle DLA care component, supporting
      a component-specific association.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch60/0004
      quote: "60033 [see DMG memo 02/25] “Severely disabled person” means a person for whom\n\n\n1. AA1 or\n\n\n\
        2. the care component of DLA at the highest or middle rate or pension age disability\npayment2 or\n\n3.
        CAA payable as\n\n\n       3.1 an increase of IIDB3 or\n\n\n       3.2 an increase of an old scheme allowance4
        or\n\n\n       3.3 an increase of WC5 or\n\n\n       3.4 a WDisP6 or\n\n\n4. the daily living component
        of PIP at the standard or enhanced rate 7 or"
      locator: DMG 60033
